The placement of this matcher feels arbitrary. Would have expected it to be either the first or last so that the name based matchers would be grouped. An alternative could be to add 
```java
  public static ElementMatcher<? super Iterable<? extends TypeDescription>> names(String... names) {
    return types -> {
      Iterator<? extends TypeDescription> i = types.iterator();
      for (String name : names) {
        if (!i.hasNext()) {
          return false;
        }
        TypeDescription type = i.next();
        if (!name.equals(type.getName())) {
          return false;
        }
      }
      return !i.hasNext();
    };
  }
```
to `AgentElementMatchers` so we could use `takesArgument(names("a", "b"))` and wouldn't need an explicit argument count check. Idk if that would help. Didn't test whether this works at all.

